{
  "module": "Input side: text to vectors",
  "lesson": {
    "slug": "sequence-shapes",
    "title": "Sequence length and reading shapes",
    "summary": "How many tokens are in a text, what the context window limits, and how to read the shape n × d_model and the course's symbols.",
    "covers": [
      "sequence-length",
      "shape-notation"
    ],
    "prerequisites": [
      {
        "lesson": "tokens",
        "reason": "n counts tokens, so you need to know what a token is first."
      }
    ]
  },
  "screens": [
    {
      "ref": "n",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Once text has been split into tokens, the first number you need is how many there are. That count is called the "
            },
            {
              "text": "sequence length",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", written "
            },
            {
              "text": "n",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "A sentence that becomes 7 tokens has n = 7. A whole page that becomes 600 tokens has n = 600."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "note",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "n counts "
            },
            {
              "text": "tokens",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", not words and not characters. The same sentence can have a different n under a different tokenizer."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 5)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "window",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "A model cannot take in an unlimited number of tokens. The most it can handle at once is called its "
            },
            {
              "text": "context window",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ": the maximum n it supports."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The window has to hold everything: "
            },
            {
              "text": "the prompt plus everything the model generates",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ". If the window is 1,000 tokens and your prompt already uses 900, the model has room for at most 100 more."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "note",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "This is why a very long conversation eventually stops working: n has reached the window."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 5)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "table",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Later in the course each token will be represented by a list of numbers, all the same length. Do not worry yet about what those numbers mean. For now we only need the "
            },
            {
              "text": "shape",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": " they make."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Put those lists on top of each other, one per token, and you get a table of numbers with "
            },
            {
              "text": "one row per token",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ". In maths a table like this is a "
            },
            {
              "text": "matrix",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 7)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "shape",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The size of a matrix is written "
            },
            {
              "text": "rows × columns",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ". In this course the sequence is written "
            },
            {
              "text": "n × d_model",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ":"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "text": "n",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": " rows: one for each token in the sequence"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "d_model",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": " columns: the length of each token's list of numbers (the next lesson explains where it comes from)"
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "So n × d_model means "
            },
            {
              "text": "n tokens, each represented by a d_model-long vector",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 7)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "example",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "A worked example with small made-up numbers: 5 tokens, and each token's list is 4 numbers long."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "text": "Written as a shape: "
              },
              {
                "text": "5 × 4",
                "bold": true
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "Rows: 5 (one per token)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "Columns: 4 (the length of each list)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "Total numbers in the table: 5 × 4 = 20"
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "If the sequence grew to 6 tokens, the table would gain one row and become 6 × 4. The number of columns does not change with the text."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 7)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "symbols",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The course uses a small set of symbols and explains each one in full where it first appears. Here is the list to come back to:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "text": "n",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": ": sequence length"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "V",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": ": vocabulary size"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "d_model",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": ": width of the token vectors"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "L",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": ": number of transformer layers (blocks)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "h",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": ": number of attention heads"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "d_k",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": ", "
              },
              {
                "text": "d_v",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": ": per-head query/key size and value size"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "d_ff",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": ": hidden width of the feed-forward sublayer"
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "note",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "One deliberate exception: when we reach the rule of thumb for training compute, "
            },
            {
              "text": "N",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " is the number of parameters and "
            },
            {
              "text": "D",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " is the number of training tokens."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 8)"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "questions": [
    {
      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "What does the sequence length n count?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "options": [
        {
          "correct": true,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "The tokens in the sequence being processed"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "n is the number of tokens, whatever the tokenizer made of the text."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "The words in the text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "Words are not the unit. A word can be one token or several."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "The characters in the text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "Characters are not counted; a token can hold several characters."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "The number of tokens in the vocabulary"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "That is V, the vocabulary size, not n."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "teaches": [
        "n"
      ],
      "covers": [
        "sequence-length"
      ],
      "variants": [
        {
          "prompt": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "A text is turned into 12 tokens. Which symbol stands for 12?"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "options": [
            {
              "correct": true,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "n, the sequence length"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "reason": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "n is how many tokens are in the sequence being processed."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "correct": false,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "V, the vocabulary size"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "reason": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "V is how many different tokens the model knows, not how many are in this text."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "correct": false,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "d_model, the width of the vectors"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "reason": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "d_model is the length of each token's vector, not the number of tokens."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "correct": false,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "L, the number of layers"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "reason": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "L counts the model's layers, not the tokens in a text."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
